31	/**
32	 * Merges one person into another (a steward only; neither retired, not the same person). The merged person's claims
33	 * move to the other, keeping their numbers and dates, listed after the other's in the order they were added and
34	 * keeping any figure a statement bound; their name and aliases become the other's aliases; their patrons are added to
35	 * the other's and anyone naming them as patron names the other instead (never themselves, never twice); their pool
36	 * memberships move to the other (shares added where the other is a member already); their statements are counted
37	 * with the other's, whose last statement stays theirs (or, having none, becomes the merged person's last). Their
38	 * holds, watchers, plans and contact are dropped, and the merged person is kept aside, off the sheet.
39	 *
40	 * <p>The last merge into a person can be undone by the steward who made it, on the sheet's today it was made: the
41	 * merged person is back at the end of the list with the claims that came from them (as they are now, in their places
42	 * before) and their own aliases, which leave the other's; patron, pool and crew changes stay.
43	 */
